Equipment Setup & Operation Protocol
    1. Laptop & Arduino Setup
          Open the laptop.
          Connect the buttons to the laptop.
          Open Arduino IDE.
          The file DiscoverDay.ino should open automatically.
          Click the checkmark (✓) to verify the code.
          Click the arrow (→) to upload the code.
          
          If there are errors:
          Go to Tools → Board and ensure “Arduino Mega or Mega 2560” is selected.
          Check Tools → Port and note which COM port is being used (e.g., COM4).
          Close Arduino IDE when finished.

    2. Python Program Setup
          Open Visual Studio Code.
          The file DiscoverDay.py should open automatically.
          Confirm the correct COM port is listed on line 17 (must match Arduino).

    3. Phone & Glasses Setup
          Connect the glasses to the Samsung phone.
          Unlock the phone.
          Turn on the mobile hotspot.
          On the laptop, connect to the phone’s hotspot.

    4. Neon Companion App Setup
          On the phone, open the Neon Companion app.
          Find the IP address in the app.
          Ensure this IP address matches the one listed on line 56 in the Python code.
    
    5. Running the Experiment
          In Visual Studio Code, click the Play (▶) button (top right).
          Wait 1–2 minutes for connections:
          Arduino should connect
          Phone should connect
          Click Start:
              A beep will play
              A button will light up
              Neon glasses begin recording
              The system will:
                    Cycle through beeps and buttons
                    Continue recording automatically
          Click Stop to end recording.
          
    6. Saving Data
          After exiting, data is saved as an Excel file in the Downloads folder.
          To find it:
          Open File Explorer → Downloads
          The file should be the most recent item
    
    7. Uploading to Pupil Cloud
          Ensure the phone is connected to eduroam Wi-Fi.
          In the Neon Companion app, tap the cloud icon to upload the recording.
    
    8. Viewing Data
          On the laptop, open Pupil Cloud (bookmarked in browser).
          Select the uploaded recording.
          You should see:
                  A red circle indicating gaze fixation
                  A video of the participant’s eyes in the top-right corner
    
    9. Shutdown & Cleanup
          Turn off the phone’s mobile hotspot to save data.
          Disconnect all devices.

